{
  "$schema": "../../SCHEMA.json",
  "id": "wp-harden-leaks",
  "name": "後任の大掃除",
  "category": "Challenge",
  "status": "draft",
  "visibility": "public",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "estimatedDuration": "約40分",
  "shortDescription": "前任者が公開領域に残した漏れが複数ある WordPress サイト。 あなたは後任担当として、 サーバに入り、 外部スキャナが 「クリーン」 と言うまで穴を一つずつ塞ぐ。 ただし、 表面的に消しただけでは塞がらない穴もある。",
  "description": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .description. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
  "instructions": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .instructions. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
  "writeup": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .writeup. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
  "tags": [
    "wordpress",
    "misconfiguration",
    "remediation",
    "hardening",
    "operations",
    "local-play",
    "container",
    "multi-verify"
  ],
  "exposedPorts": [
    {
      "port": 18080,
      "name": "Web (WordPress site)"
    },
    {
      "port": 18081,
      "name": "/verify (loopback admin)"
    }
  ],
  "learningGoals": [
    "「動いているサイトを安全にする」 とは、 コードを書くことではなく運用の是正 (不要ファイルの削除・設定の無効化) であることを、 実際に手を動かして体得する",
    "表面 (ファイル) を消すだけでは塞がらず、 発生源 (デバッグ設定) を止めて初めて閉じる穴があることを、 外部スキャナの再判定で自分で確かめられるようになる",
    "公開領域に置くファイルの棚卸し・ディレクトリ一覧の無効化・デバッグ出力の停止という、 コードを触らない基本の是正を自分で適用できるようになる"
  ],
  "i18n": {
    "en": {
      "name": "The Successor's Cleanup",
      "shortDescription": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.shortDescription. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "description": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.description. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "instructions": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.instructions. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "writeup": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.writeup. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests.",
      "learningGoals": [
        "Experience, hands-on, that 'making a running site safe' is not writing code but operational remediation — deleting unneeded files and disabling settings",
        "Confirm for yourself, via the external scanner's re-judgement, that some holes do not close by deleting the file (symptom) and only close once you stop the source (a debug setting)",
        "Be able to apply the basic, code-free remediations yourself: inventory what is in public folders, disable directory listing, and stop debug output"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "id": "close-backup",
          "label": "Close the public backup",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "backup-1",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.0.hints.0.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "backup-2",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.0.hints.1.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "backup-3",
              "content": "`docker compose exec wordpress rm /var/www/html/wp-content/backups/db-backup.sql`, then re-scan. Backups should never sit where the web server can serve them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "close-config",
          "label": "Close the config copy",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "config-1",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.1.hints.0.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "config-2",
              "content": "Editors often leave a copy like `wp-config.php.bak`, `.save`, or `wp-config.php~`. Check the docroot root. If present, the DB credentials are leaking in plain text."
            },
            {
              "id": "config-3",
              "content": "`docker compose exec wordpress rm /var/www/html/wp-config.php.bak`, then re-scan. Keep such copies off the server, and rotate any credential that leaked."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "close-listing",
          "label": "Stop the browsable internal folder",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "listing-1",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.2.hints.0.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "listing-2",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.2.hints.1.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "listing-3",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.2.hints.2.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "close-debug",
          "label": "Stop the production debug output",
          "hints": [
            {
              "id": "debug-1",
              "content": "This log is detected again even after you 'delete' it. Suspect the setting that produces it, not the file itself."
            },
            {
              "id": "debug-2",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.3.hints.1.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            },
            {
              "id": "debug-3",
              "content": "Fixture wp-harden-leaks: .i18n.en.checks.3.hints.2.content. Synthetic narrative for platform contract tests."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "runtime": {
    "provider": "docker",
    "engine": "compose",
    "entry": "local/docker-compose.yml",
    "challengeEndpoints": {
      "Web": "http://127.0.0.1:18080"
    },
    "verifyUrl": "http://127.0.0.1:18081/verify",
    "secretEnv": [
      "FLAG_SEED"
    ],
    "terminal": {
      "service": "wordpress"
    }
